    "lyrics": "[intro]\n\n[verse]\n风把我不想知道的事情告诉我\n河把我不想忘记的故事\n也带走\n我摘下我的翅膀\n它变成白鸟\n白鸟我的白鸟\n逆着风去吧\n飞过河滩\n\n[chorus]\n挥一挥一去不回还\n一去不回还\n风起水起难靠岸\n白鸟白鸟不要回头望\n你要替我飞去那地方\n一去那地方\n那是你我共同故乡\n\n[verse]\n抓住和抓不住的照片\n哪张更美\n去过和没去过的地方\n哪里更远\n白鸟\n我的白鸟\n你要飞得更高\n不要回来\n若还想与我相见\n就来我的梦里边\n\n[chorus]\n白鸟过河滩\n挥一挥一去不回还\n一去不回还\n风起水起难靠岸\n白鸟白鸟不要回头望\n你要替我飞去那地方\n一去那地方\n那是你我共同故乡\n别回来\n我将终究顺流入大海\n顺流入大海\n海不问我从何处来\n长风长风飘在山海间\n白鸟白鸟展翅入苍天\n一去入苍天\n苍天远在海背面\n一去入苍天\n苍天远\n比海更远",
    "songName": "白鸟过河滩",
    "artist": "ilem（洛天依演唱）",
    "coverStyle": "mainstream R&B / soul",
    "originalStyle": "This track is a Mandarin-language Mandopop ballad that blends contemporary pop songwriting with a lush, orchestral-pop arrangement.\n It moves at a moderate 111 BPM in a steady 4/4 meter and is rooted in E♭ minor, giving the piece a wistful, melancholic tonality.\n\n Instrumentation & production:  The arrangement is built around a warm acoustic piano that carries the harmonic foundation, while sweeping string sections add depth and emotional weight. A smooth electric bass underpins the low end, and a gentle drum kit—featuring soft kick, brushed snare, and subtle hi-hat patterns—provides a restrained rhythmic pulse. The mix is polished and high-fidelity, with a wide stereo field that places the piano and strings expansively, while the vocals sit front-center with tasteful reverb and delay to enhance the intimate atmosphere.\n\n Vocal characteristics:  The lead is a male tenor singing in Mandarin. His timbre is clear, smooth, and highly expressive, delivering the melody with a heartfelt, lyrical style. The vocal line is treated with spacious reverb and a hint of delay, creating a sense of longing and intimacy without obscuring articulation.\n\n Lyrical themes:  The lyrics explore memory, loss, and the passage of time, using the metaphor of a “white bird” (白鳥) that flies away as a symbol of fading recollection. The chorus repeats the poignant lines:\n\n> “白鳥白鳥不要回頭望  \n> 你要替我飛去那地方  \n> 一去那地方 那是你我共同故鄉”\n\nThese lines reinforce the theme of letting go and moving toward an imagined shared homeland.\n\n Song structure & dynamics:  The composition follows a classic verse-chorus form. An intro of solo piano and ambient strings sets a reflective mood, leading into the first verse where the vocal melody is intimate and the instrumentation remains sparse. The pre-chorus builds subtly with added strings and a slightly more active drum pattern, culminating in a full-band chorus where the piano, strings, bass, and drums swell together, delivering the emotional peak. A second verse mirrors the first, followed by a repeat of the chorus, and the track concludes with a gentle outro that strips back to piano and fading strings, leaving a lingering sense of nostalgia.\n\n Theoretical grounding:  Harmonic movement centers on the tonic E♭ minor, with frequent use of the iv chord B♭ minor and the VI chord C♯ major, creating a bittersweet contrast between minor melancholy and brief moments of brighter major coloration. The progression often moves E♭m → B♭m → C♯ → F♯, which emphasizes the minor mode while providing a subtle lift before returning to the home key, reinforcing the lyrical tension between remembrance and release.\n\n Overall mood & context:  The track exudes a reflective, nostalgic aesthetic typical of early-2020s Mandopop ballads, where polished production meets emotive songwriting. Its blend of piano-driven pop sensibility with orchestral textures situates it within the tradition of Chinese pop music that values lyrical storytelling and cinematic arrangements, resonating with listeners who appreciate heartfelt narratives of love, loss, and the yearning for a shared past.",
